.TH VALIDITY-VENDOR 8 "2026-10-24" "validity-rs" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
validity-vendor \- install the Synaptics vendor files used by validity-daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validity-vendor install
.RB [ \-\-archive
.IR FILE " |"
.B \-\-url
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B validity-vendor check
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B validity-daemon
needs two files from Lenovo's Synaptics driver package
.IR nz3gf07w.exe ,
which may not be redistributed: the driver DLL, which holds the sensor command
blobs, and the sensor firmware extension.
.B validity-vendor install
downloads the package on this machine, checks its SHA\-256, extracts the two
files, checks theirs, and switches them into
.I DIR/vendor
in one atomic step. If the files are already in place and intact, it does
nothing and does not use the network. A failure leaves the previous state
untouched. The packages run it after installation; run it again by hand
(as root) if the machine was offline then.
.PP
.B validity-vendor check
reports whether the files are in place and intact.
.PP
Password login never depends on these files: without them the fingerprint
sensor is simply unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-archive " FILE"
Use a copy of
.I nz3gf07w.exe
already on disk, for example one downloaded on another machine. No network is
used.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Download from
.I URL
(a mirror) instead of Lenovo. The SHA\-256 check is the same.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Installation directory, default
.IR /var/lib/validity .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VALIDITY_VENDOR_URL
Default for
.BR \-\-url .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done or already in place, 1 error, 2 usage error, 3 download failed,
4 (check) files missing or damaged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/validity/vendor
Link to the installed set of files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/validity-rs/validity-rs
.UE
